# WARDEN — CCDC Linux Defense & Forensic Quarantine Suite

Automated competition-day Linux hardening, persistent `nftables` firewall enforcement (default-deny inbound & outbound), and continuous intrusion monitoring (`warden.service`) with an interactive admin CLI (`gatekeeper`) and automated Incident Report (IR) forensic packet generation.

## Repository Files (`CCDC-Test/Warden/`)
* **`setup.py`** — **Run this first.** Auto-detects the host profile (`rocky`, `ubuntu`, `debian`), rotates `sysadmin` and `root` passwords, masks `ufw`/`firewalld`, enforces `gatekeeper_fw.sh`, initializes `/opt/warden/warden.db`, configures the Splunk Universal Forwarder (with interactive Indexer IP/port prompts), and installs `warden.service` and `gatekeeper`.
* **`gatekeeper_fw.sh`** — Bootstraps `nftables` with default-drop inbound and outbound policies, ICMP ping support (Rule 12), and reboot persistence on both Debian/Ubuntu (`/etc/nftables.conf`) and Rocky/RHEL (`/etc/sysconfig/nftables.conf`).
* **`warden_daemon.py`** — Background service (`/usr/bin/warden_daemon.py`) that freezes (`SIGSTOP`) active reverse-shell/C2 processes instead of destroying evidence, generates ready-to-submit Incident Report bundles in `/opt/warden/quarantine/`, locks unauthorized accounts, reverts `/etc/crontab` tampering (saving evidence first), and monitors shell binary SHA-256 integrity.
* **`gatekeeper.py`** — Interactive CLI (`/usr/bin/gatekeeper`) for banning Red Team IPs/CIDRs, whitelisting Blue Team jump hosts, opening/closing inject ports, and flagging rogue users or services live.
* **`warden.service`** — Systemd unit file installed to `/etc/systemd/system/warden.service`.

---

## Quick Start (Competition Day)

### 1. Clone & Deploy (Run First)
Run as `root` (or with `sudo`) on each Linux server (`Rocky Ecom .10`, `Ubuntu Email .15`, `Debian Splunk .20`):
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/thomasbrady10-cyber/CCDC-Test.git](https://github.com/thomasbrady10-cyber/CCDC-Test.git) /opt/CCDC-Test
cd /opt/CCDC-Test/Warden
sudo python3 setup.py
